  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want an independent code-quality review of SwiftHFR by **Fable 5.2** (or the latest Fable at the time) at the end of M4, so that the code is reliable, consistent, maintainable, well factored and well commented, with algorithms that are simple and right, before release. Operator request, 2026-11-10.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #774\n\n\n### When\nEnd of M4, **second** of two sequential reviews: starts only after review 1/2 (#774, performance) is closed. `status: blocked` until then.\n\n### Scope\nApp (`App/SwiftHFR`) and engine (`Packages/HFRKit`), tests and tooling where they carry logic:\n- **Reliability**: error paths, cancellation and races (async/await, `@MainActor`, loaders), state that survives relaunch and upgrades (ESSENTIEL persistence rule), flaky tests (#704, #772) as symptoms.\n- **Consistency**: one way to do the same thing (lists, loaders, settings, navigation, accessibility), naming, the conventions of AGENTS §4.\n- **Maintainability**: module boundaries (ARCHITECTURE), file and type size, dead code, duplication, speculative abstractions, test quality (tests that fail without the change).\n- **Factoring level**: missing or excessive shared components.\n- **Comments**: \"why\" comments present, no \"what\" noise, legacy pointers (AGENTS §4) accurate.\n- **Algorithm quality**: correctness, complexity, clarity — the simplest right algorithm.\n\n### Method\n- Independent of the authors (AGENTS §6): the reviewer reads the code, specs and LESSONS, not the authors' conclusions.\n- Every finding is a claim checked against the code (file:line) and, where possible, a failing test or a measured case.\n\n### Output\n- One comment on this issue: the ranked list of findings by theme.\n- **One issue per finding** (or per coherent group), each with: `### Summary` (intent), the code to review (`file:line`), the test that proves it (failing before the fix), the definition of done, and the **ideal model for the rework** (AGENTS §6 routing), with labels on every axis. Learnings that apply to future work go to LESSONS by PR.\n- No code change in this issue.\n\n### Definition of done\n- [ ] Every theme above reviewed; every finding filed as above; this issue closed with the list.\n\nDepends on #774.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
